The Problem: 
Heat sensors and radar can confirm a physical event, but relying entirely on abiotic (non-living) sensors can still leave room for doubt.The Solution: Animals react to environmental disasters long before standard sensors cross critical thresholds. HELIOS incorporates a Wildlife Indicator. By monitoring local fauna, a sudden mass exodus, unusual clustering, or complete absence of wildlife acts as a highly reliable, independent biological signal that something is wrong.

The Action:

To preserve power, this camera node stays completely offline.

Once Layer 2 (Radar) detects sustained physical disturbance, it wakes up the Layer 3 camera.

The Edge AI runs a lightweight YOLOv8 object detection model.

It scans the frame specifically for Biological Anomalies (e.g., an abnormal count of animals in the frame, simulating fleeing wildlife) alongside visual hazard confirmation.

If the biological anomaly is verified, it publishes the final HAZARD_VERIFIED payload to dispatch the UAV.
