Implementation:
Hackathon Software:

Python & OpenCV: To control the webcam and handle image frames.

YOLOv8 (Ultralytics): An ultra-fast, state-of-the-art object detection model.

The Hackathon Trick: Training a custom model for "wildlife fleeing" takes weeks. Instead, we use the pre-trained YOLOv8 Nano (yolov8n.pt) model, which is trained on the COCO dataset. It natively recognizes animals like bird, cat, dog, horse, sheep, and cow. We will write a logic rule: If the camera detects multiple animals suddenly appearing (simulating a fleeing herd) after a radar trigger, confirm the hazard.

3. The Python Code Implementation
This script subscribes to the MQTT broker. Upon receiving the MOTION_CONFIRMED trigger from the Radar, it turns on the webcam, runs YOLOv8, counts the biological subjects, and triggers the drone if an anomaly is detected.
